'Guanine nucleotide-binding protein G(I)/G(S)/G(T) subunit beta-1 with n-terminal his-tag and 3C cleavage site and GSSG linker' 
3 polymer     man 'Guanine nucleotide-binding protein G(I)/G(S)/G(O) subunit gamma-2' 8506.765  1 ? ? ? ? 
4 polymer     man 'Soluble cytochrome b562,5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1A,5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1A' 61375.930 1 ? 3 ? 
;N-terminal HA signal sequence, flag-tag, his-tag, tev cleavage site followed by soluble cytochrome b562 (E. coli) and truncated 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1A (Homo sapiens) with a point mutation at position 255 in the provided sequence. This mutation is Ballesteros-Weinstein position 3.41 of 5-HT1A where the original leucine was mutated to a tryptophan. Cytochrome b562 (cybC, UniProt P0ABE7) is both n and c-terminally truncated with two point mutations.,N-terminal HA signal sequence, flag-tag, his-tag, tev cleavage site followed by soluble cytochrome b562 (E. coli) and truncated 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1A (Homo sapiens) with a point mutation at position 255 in the provided sequence. This mutation is Ballesteros-Weinstein position 3.41 of 5-HT1A where the original leucine was mutated to a tryptophan. Cytochrome b562 (cybC, UniProt P0ABE7) is both n and c-terminally truncated with two point mutations.
;
